  "sourceReview": {
    "currentApi": "ReadLease.current(index) checks closed/capacity/occupancy under held shared lock and returns current generation. Correct for instance-local index-only lookup; deliberately does not detect stale native integer IDs after reuse.",
    "relay": "CALL rel32 targets near leaf relay at stub+0x100. MOVABS RAX,actual C++ helper; JMP RAX allows helper outside2GiB without changing stack or return address. Relay is leaf with no stack allocation; helper has compiler-generated unwind metadata. Entry now uses absolute transfer.",
    "allocation": "64KiB-aligned reservations are separate; absolute requested reservation mismatch fails and releases only newly acquired memory. Executable protection/cache flush precede calls. Tables are destroyed before mapped code/metadata windows.",
    "callbacks": "Synthetic callback table remains live for every call, matched retain/release IDs are asserted, absent callbacks and foreign Mission rejected. No engine callback implementation loaded.",
    "teardown": "Single-thread ordering closes storage before active_storage=null, releases objects, unregisters both tables then frees regions. Fault-injection confirms pre-call registration failure cleanup; active_storage global would be dangling after a later exceptional exit, but harness exits immediately without later lookups."
  },
